[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116414,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A dermoid cyst is a developmental cystic lesion composed of ectodermal and mesodermal tissues, typically including epidermis-like squamous epithelium and cutaneous adnexal structures. A teratoid cyst includes endodermal tissues.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116415,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116416,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DA05.Y Other specified cysts of oral or facial-neck region &amp; Dermoid cyst of mouth</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116417,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> dermoid; cystic dermoid; cystic teratoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116418,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116419,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 7% of all dermoid cysts are found in the head and neck region {32884763}, most commonly in the periorbital region, as well as in the orbit, ear, dorsum of the nose, floor of the mouth&nbsp;/ submental region, and the mid-neck region.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116420,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a nonspecific, firm, palpable mass. They may present with a cutaneous pit secreting sebaceous material and with protruding hair follicles.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Imaging studies are recommended for ruling out osseous or intracranial extension. In the floor of the mouth&nbsp;/ submandibular region, imaging may reveal a well-defined lesion, classically containing intracystic corpuscles (the sack-of-marbles sign), that is hypodense on CT, hyperintense on T1-weighted MRI and low-signal on T2-weighted MRI due to lipid content. Occasionally these &ldquo;marbles&rdquo; may be calcified. Such imaging features permit differentiation from simple cystic lesions (e.g. ranula) in these anatomical sites {21918039}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116421,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is an equivocal sex predilection (a possible slight female preponderance). These cysts are often present from birth, with approximately 70% diagnosed in patients aged &lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;years {25439551; 30466230}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116422,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermoid and teratoid cysts are developmental cystic lesions. There is no reported genetic etiology.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116423,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cysts most commonly arise due to entrapped ectoderm and mesoderm along planes of embryonic fusion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116424,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are cystic lesions as large as 120&nbsp;mm and commonly filled with keratinaceous debris {32884763}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116425,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The dermoid cyst wall is composed of keratinized, epidermis-like squamous epithelium. Abundant desquamated keratin or hair follicles may be noted within the cystic lumen. Cutaneous adnexal structures are present in the underlying connective tissues and possibly attached to the cyst wall, and they may include hair follicles or sebaceous, eccrine, or apocrine glandular elements. Teratoid cyst includes endodermal tissues, to potentially include gastrointestinal or respiratory epithelium, or glandular tissues to include pancreatic or salivary tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116426,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cysts may contain desquamated anucleate and nucleated squamous epithelial cells and keratin debris {10352915}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116427,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116428,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<p>Dermoid cyst: a squamous epithelium&ndash;lined cystic lesion with associated adnexal structures, possibly including hair follicles and glandular elements (sebaceous, eccrine, and/or apocrine).</p>\r\n<p>Teratoid cyst: same as above, but including endodermal tissues such as respiratory or gastrointestinal mucosa.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116429,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116430,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 270,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrence is unusual.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T13:33:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
